// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/course/queen-and-hive.t27 -- the t27 course on the Queen and the hive, how the project builds itself
; Source of truth for apps/website/scripts/course-from-spec.mjs (gHashTag/trinity), which reads
; it the way it reads specs/course/course.t27: the constant schema, every test block below, every
; widget in specs/widgets/gallery.t27, every lesson spec compiled clean, the Russian bundle named
; by specs/course/queen-and-hive-ru.t27. It writes this course into src/lib/course.generated.ts
; (the page at #/queen-and-hive) and a byte-identical copy of this file at
; public/learn/queen-and-hive.t27. ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT THE COURSE IS: course 11 of specs/course/courses.t27, 27 lessons in 9 modules of 3: the
; task, who goes next, a bee's life, the reviewer bee, the review jam, keys, credit and money,
; agents among themselves, and night and the board. The project builds itself: an issue becomes
; a task for a bee, the bee writes a .t27 spec, a reviewer bee checks it, it merges and the site
; regenerates. The Queen that runs this loop is written in gHashTag/t27 specs/queen and
; specs/automation, each spec with numeric tests. Every widget runs the fn bodies of one of 15 of
; those specs compiled to WebAssembly (public/widgets/<id>/logic.js, held to its spec by
; scripts/widget-logic.mjs), vendored byte for byte from t27 master c42f8fb40. The door code
; around review-jam's fns comes from gHashTag/999-multibots-telegraf#4020.

; WHAT THE COURSE DOES NOT DO: it reads no live Queen. Every number in a lesson is a constant or
; a recorded measurement of the lesson spec, or an answer of its compiled fns to inputs the
; reader sets. Lesson 26 shows a finding of dispatch.t27 as the board draws it today: a closed
; issue's finished claims all land in done.

; WHY 27: 3 cubed lessons, the size of a TRI-27 word. Changing the shape changes the tests.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module queen_and_hive;

